    "notes": "Dictionary form -> simple past, for the verbs a regular -ed rule gets wrong. WordNet's exception list only goes the other way (led -> lead) and does not say which irregular form is the past and which the participle, so re-inflecting a synonym into the past tense needs this map; without it the lookup had to drop every irregular synonym rather than offer \"taked\". Only the simple past is kept, because bullets are written in it. The data-integrity test checks every pair against the vendored WordNet exception list."
